Package: wayland-vnc-grd
Architecture: any
Depends:
 ${shlibs:Depends},
 ${misc:Depends},
 gnome-remote-desktop
Enhances: wayland-vnc
Description: GNOME Remote Desktop VNC backend, patched, for wayland-vnc
 The project's private build of GNOME Remote Desktop 50.2 and LibVNCServer 0.9.15
 with the wayland-vnc patch series: no crash when a client disconnects, the colour
 depth the encoder really uses, hung-up clients dropped from the connection queue,
 every client message processed before an update is sent, and the PipeWire data
 loop kept off the realtime scheduler so a 4K stream is not killed by the
 watchdog. Installed under /opt/wayland-vnc and run in place of the distribution
 daemon through a systemd user drop-in; the distribution package stays installed,
 and removing this one puts it back.
 .
 Built from the checksum-pinned upstream tarballs vendored in this source package
 (sources.json in the wayland-vnc repository), so it builds without network access.
